  "body": {
    "id": "thm:global-risk-band",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "The band \\(C_n\\) is measurable and satisfies \\(\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}\\inf_{P\\in\\mathcal M_n}\\Pr_P\\{R_P(v)\\in C_n(v)\\text{ for every }v\\in\\Delta_K\\}\\ge1-\\alpha\\), together with the explicit uniform stochastic diameter bound \\(\\lim_{M_{\\mathrm{wid}}\\to\\infty}\\limsup_{n\\to\\infty}\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal M_n}\\Pr_P\\{\\sup_{v\\in\\Delta_K}\\sqrt n\\,\\operatorname{diam}C_n(v)>M_{\\mathrm{wid}}\\}=0\\). Hence every measurable same-panel selector \\(\\widehat v\\in\\Delta_K\\) obeys \\(\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}\\inf_{P\\in\\mathcal M_n}\\Pr_P\\{R_P(\\widehat v)\\in C_n(\\widehat v)\\}\\ge1-\\alpha\\), including sequences within \\(O(n^{-1/2})\\) of any donor-face change.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Cn",
      "n",
      "P",
      "ModelClass",
      "RP",
      "v",
      "DeltaK",
      "alpha",
      "Mwidth"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "lem:global-parameterization",
      "ass:bounded-signals",
      "ass:rank-spectrum",
      "def:global-moment-region",
      "def:global-risk-band",
      "lem:row-span-completion",
      "prop:kkt-stratification",
      "lem:joint-moment-expansion"
    ],
    "justification": "This is the first same-panel certificate for the entire population prediction-risk graph and automatically protects unsplit predictor tuning.",
    "gap": "VivesiBastida2022PredictorSelection and PouliotXieLiu2026DegreesFreedom tune predictors without an honest full-risk-graph band; CanenSong2026SimplexWeight covers a fixed objective rather than a continuum whose donor face moves.",
    "consumer": "An implementation of the displayed fixed-ridge quadratic simplex estimator can compare predictor weights and retain a valid risk certificate after selecting one on the same pre panel; the theorem does not certify the different objectives implemented by Synth or SparseSC.",
    "proof_tex": "This proof uses the corrected empty-set convention proposed for Definition \\(\\mathrm{def:global\\mbox{-}risk\\mbox{-}band}\\). By Lemma \\(\\mathrm{lem:joint\\mbox{-}moment\\mbox{-}expansion}\\), uniformly over \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_n\\),\n\\[\n\\widehat V^{-1/2}\\sqrt n\\{\\widehat z-z(\\theta_P)\\}\\Longrightarrow N(0,I_{q_z}),\n\\]\nwhere \\(\\theta_P\\) represents \\(P\\). Hence\n\\[\n\\liminf_n\\inf_{P\\in\\mathcal M_n}\\Pr_P\\{\\theta_P\\in E_n\\}\\geq1-\\alpha.\n\\]\nOn that event, simultaneously for every \\(v\\in\\Delta_K\\), \\(R_P(v)=R_{P_{\\theta_P}}(v)\\in C_n(v)\\).\n\nFor diameter, the fixed-rank spectral bound gives \\(\\|\\widetilde A^+-A^+\\|\\leq C\\|\\widetilde A-A\\|\\) for close legal signals. Adding the two optimizer variational inequalities gives\n\\[\n2\\rho\\|\\widetilde w(v)-w(v)\\|^2\n\\leq\\langle\\{H(v)-\\widetilde H(v)\\}w(v)+\\widetilde f(v)-f(v),\\widetilde w(v)-w(v)\\rangle.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\|w(v)\\|\\leq1\\), \\(S\\) is bounded, and \\(v\\in\\Delta_K\\),\n\\[\n\\sup_{v\\in\\Delta_K}\\|\\widetilde w(v)-w(v)\\|\\leq C\\|\\widetilde z-z\\|,\n\\qquad\n\\sup_{v\\in\\Delta_K}|R_{\\widetilde\\theta}(v)-R_\\theta(v)|\\leq C_R\\|\\widetilde z-z\\|.\n\\]\nNo strict complementarity is used.\n\nWhen \\(\\widehat V\\) has eigenvalues in a fixed compact subinterval of \\((0,\\infty)\\), every two elements of nonempty \\(E_n\\) satisfy \\(\\|z(\\theta)-z(\\widetilde\\theta)\\|\\leq C/\\sqrt n\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\sup_{v\\in\\Delta_K}\\sqrt n\\,\\operatorname{diam}C_n(v)\\leq C.\n\\]\nUniform consistency of \\(\\widehat V\\) makes the complementary event vanish uniformly. If \\(E_n=\\varnothing\\), the corrected interval has diameter zero. The feasible signal set is a finite union of bounded closed rank charts and the criterion is continuous on each chart, so finite-chart measurable minimization gives measurable endpoints. This proves coverage, measurability, and the stochastic diameter statement. On the same simultaneous event, \\(R_P(\\widehat v)\\in C_n(\\widehat v)\\) for every measurable \\(\\widehat v\\); uniformity includes selectors within \\(O(n^{-1/2})\\) of face changes.",
